It is evening.
I am getting down from the bus.
I am walking towards my house.
There is a lot of crowd on the street.
I stop near a small shop.
I want fresh milk and bread.
A man is working in the shop.
I politely call him 'Dada'.
"Dada, give me one packet of milk," I say.
"And give me one packet of bread too."
"Yes, Madam," he says.
He is giving me the milk and bread.
"How much is it, Dada?" I ask.
"Sixty rupees, Madam," he says.
I am taking money out of my purse.
I give him sixty rupees.
He smiles and takes the money.
I put the things in my bag.
Now I am walking towards my house again.
